This was, simply, my ugliest ascension to date.  It was also my first
on NAO, which means that the TTYREC is available for anyone who wants
to watch it
(http://alt.org/nethack/ttyrec/Thvor/2006-10-08.02:40:46.ttyrec); the
interesting stuff happened after I got to the water plane, on turn
61952.  But I'll start with the background.

My previous two ascensions were a neutral barbarian and a lawful valk;
it seemed appropriate to do a wizard next, and the RNG made me elven,
which was nice--I don't remember if I started with 20 Int, but I got
there quickly and enjoyed it.  The beginning game was fairly
uneventful; Izchak only had candles, but that was ok with me--I'd
decided that wizards, between the polymorph spell and magicbane, were
ideal candidates for wishless and genoless conducts, and so would've
only used a magic lamp as a light source. As it was, I spent most of
the game up through the quest in the dark; I finally found a book of
light just before killing the Dark One.

One early boost was the magic marker I found in the mines, which was
used to write a book of identify once I'd maxed out my luck at a
convenient altar; the remaining charges went to scrolls (mostly enchant
weapon & armor).  That altar was my base for pretty much the entire
game--it gave me Magicbane and a lot of spellbooks (including the
finger, when I got crowned).  It also gave me Ogresmasher, but I
forgave it for that one.  Being able to cast create sacrifice was very
nice.  (Incidentally, I tucked Juiblex and another named demon--I
forget which one--into Sokoban when they were generated from same-race
sacrifices.  Chaotics have all the fun.)

I fought my way up to level 13, and then found a book of magic mapping,
which helped me find the portal to Ludious.  Slaughtering the hoardes
there got me over the cap to 14, and two of the four dragons there
dropped scales--a gray one and a silver one.  Not having any need for
another source of MR, I turned the silver scales into mail, and wore
them for the rest of the game.  I did get several other sets of scales
of various colors, but those got stashed, and eventually left behind.

The quest was easy; I woke up the Dark One, and then teleported to the
stairs before he could (hello, teleport control!).  That level really
ought to be no teleport, but then I would've just thwacked him one
level up, I guess.

When I got to the castle, I was amused to find the wand was fully
charged--my previous two ascensions, where I hadn't been avoiding
wishes, both featured a (0:1) castle wand.  (Incidentally, gain energy
potions were smoky; I think the RNG was mocking my decision to go
wishless.)  It was silver, so I thought about using it to smack demons
around, but I ended up just keeping it tucked safely in my BoH, which
turned out to be a good thing.

Gehennom was extremely straightforward; the big upside was that I
learned the joys of charm monster--a lich summoned a few big nasties
around me, and I quickly had some new pets.  I spent a while riding a
jabberwock; when he died, I switched to a green dragon, and eventually
upgraded to a random ki-rin that was generated on one of my passes
through the Castle level.  I was annoyed to find that my Ki-rin
wouldn't pick up armor while I was riding her; I ended up having to
re-tame her several times in the course of getting her equipped (and
getting plucked off her by engulfing monsters).

Orcus got stoned by a rubber chicken he'd summoned for me; that was
fun.

I found another wand of wishing (0:2) and a random wand of death deep
in gehennom, both of which were stashed for a rainy day.  The
wizard-sanctum run went smoothly, though I shed my pets on the way up
through the dungeon; the nice ones tended to be eating when I wanted to
go upstairs, and I didn't want to wait for them.  Surely a dragon and a
purple worm can eat faster than that, right?

Rodney showed up for the second time at the plane of earth, and was
quickly dispatched--though my first death ray missed him four times.
Confused gold detection, and I was on my way.  Air was similarly easy;
since I was riding a flying ki-rin, I didn't have to worry about
movement, and the air elementals fell to polymorph and wands of death.
Fire was also straightforward, though I lost my ki-rin there to the
monster's passive attacks--is there any way I could've gotten her fire
resistance?  Luckily, I was wearing fireproof water-walking boots, so I
didn't worry about the difference between lava and land.

Water's where it all broke down.  I used confused gold detection to
find the portal, and then started hunting for it, but I simply couldn't
find it.  I was surprised when I was told "You hear some noises in the
distance", since I didn't have any pets left, and wasn't causing
conflict.  I *think* it was actually Rodney booming out his revival
speech, but I'm not sure.  I do know that I was suddenly surrounded by
monsters, including a pair of gremlins, and I panicked--it was solid
night on NAO, and I'm paranoid about losing intrinsics.  I know, I
shouldn't have been at that point, but...I cast charm monster, and won
one of the gremlins over to my side.  The other one died very quickly.
My first hint that that wasn't ideal was when my new pet started
multiplying, swiftly.

Rodney appeared next to me, double-troubled, and stole the Amulet and
the Eye; I hurled spells at him, killing one copy--and hearing lots of
"You kill it!  You hear the rumble of distant thunder!"  Crap, I'm
killing my pet gremlins, and dropping my alignment & luck through the
floor.  After killing all the Rodneys around me (the dump indicates
that three died on the water plane, though I only remember two), I
stopped to take stock of the situation.

I was in the middle of the water plane, probably negative luck and
alignment, no Amulet, and no Eye; for some reason, I thought Rodney had
taken my Magicbane as well, though upon reflection, I realize that
can't happen--he doesn't have any interest in it.  Because stuff flows
around on water, I was worried I wouldn't be able to find either before
Rodney showed up again, much less before I found the portal.  And the
level was quickly filling up with tame gremlins, making any searching
even more difficult.

I decided to break the conducts I'd so proudly kept up to that point.
I pulled out the castle wand, wished for a pair of blessed genocide
scrolls, read one--and got some more gremlins sent in.  Dangit, my luck
really was negative; the scrolls were cursed.  Luckily, I knew remove
curse, and the second scroll wiped out all gremlins.  Since I didn't
think I had a weapon, I also wished up Stormbringer, though I only
asked for +1 in case it came in negative due to my luck.  Third zap,
nothing.  Recharged.  Fourth zap, got a couple of scrolls of gold
detection, swiftly uncursed.

About this time, the bubble expanded and I saw an amulet sitting on top
of a pile of stuff.  I swiftly moved towards it, but was beat by a
green dragon that swooped in to grab the amulet; when he picked it up,
I saw that it was the right one (named REAL, thankfully!), so I quickly
named him "TARGET" and chased him down.  Got the amulet back, and
started to think there might be some hope for this game after all.  A
little later, an iron golem dropped the Eye; if I'd realized I still
had magicbane, I would've realized I was back up to my normal strength,
but I didn't.  After using the two gold detection scrolls, I found the
portal--hiding under a pancake.  I *hate* how the portal hides under
items!

When I got to astral, I put on my blindfold, and found several
arch-liches; I really didn't want to bother with them, especially
without magicbane, and I'd already broken my conducts, so I swiftly
wished up a pair of genocide scrolls, blessed them, and took out L.
Since my alignment and luck had been drained on water, I didn't have
any pets at all (not even the angel), so I went ahead and slapped on a
ring of conflict.  I was to the right, so I went that way first;
Pestilence was guarding the neutral altar.  Dang.  Went back to the
center, where Famine was guarding...the lawful altar.  Grr.  Headed
back to the left, teleporting as much stuff out of my way as possible;
someone else killed Death for me, so I made it to the altar and
#offered.  No conducts intact, nor any shreds of my dignity, but I made
it.

